# npm audit policy: fail on critical only (audit-level sets the exit code, not what
# `npm audit` reports). Re-check on every dependency upgrade, and tighten this to "high"
# or "moderate" once the findings below clear.
#
# As of aws-cdk-lib 2.277.0 and aws-cdk 2.1148.1 (the latest releases) `npm audit`
# reports 38 findings, 36 high and 2 moderate, from two root causes. Neither can be
# fixed by upgrading yet:
#
# - GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf (CVE-2026-112366, high): picomatch <= 4.0.7, ReDoS through
#   single-branch repeated extglobs. 4.0.7 is the latest release and the advisory lists
#   no patched version. Dev-only: it reaches the tree through the jest toolchain (jest,
#   ts-jest, micromatch, anymatch), which accounts for all 36 high findings. Nothing
#   that is deployed uses it. Clears when a patched picomatch is released.
#
# - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (CVE-2026-118764, moderate): minimatch <11.0.1, DoS through glob
#   pattern amplification. Two findings (minimatch and aws-cdk-lib), and the only ones in
#   production dependencies (`npm audit --omit=dev`). The vulnerable copy (10.2.6) is
#   bundled inside aws-cdk-lib, and npm overrides do not apply to bundled dependencies.
#   Tested again on 2.277.0: an override adds a top-level minimatch 11.0.9 and leaves
#   the bundled copy untouched. aws/aws-cdk PR #39595 bumps the bundled copy to 11.0.8.
#   It merged to main on 2026-11-13, after 2.277.0 was cut, so no release contains it
#   yet. CDK uses minimatch at synth time on this repository's own paths, not on
#   untrusted patterns. Clears on the first aws-cdk-lib release that includes that PR.
#   Re-run `npm audit` after the next CDK upgrade.
#
# Do not run "npm audit fix --force": it proposes downgrading aws-cdk-lib to 2.239.0.
# A deepmerge advisory (GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4) that earlier versions of this note listed
# was withdrawn on 2026-11-16 and no longer applies.
audit-level=critical
